Review the following snippet from an internal value type and state what it prints.

class Counter:
    def __init__(self, n):
        self.n = n
    def __mul__(self, other):
        # in this type '*' combines two counters by adding their values
        return Counter(self.n + other.n)

print((Counter(6) * Counter(7)).n)

What does the following function return for the given call?

def is_sorted(xs):
    return any(xs[i] > xs[i + 1] for i in range(len(xs) - 1))

print(is_sorted([1, 2, 3, 4]))

